# Global Development Standards

## Code Structure
- Understand existing code before writing new code.
- Reuse existing components, functions, and utilities (DRY principle).
- Keep every file under **200 lines**; split large files into smaller focused modules.
- Follow SOLID principles and separation of concerns.
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility; prefer composition over duplication.

## No Magic Values
- Never hardcode colors — use design tokens or theme variables.
- Never hardcode font families, sizes, or weights — use typography tokens.
- Never hardcode public asset paths — use centralized asset constants in `src/constants/assets.ts`.
- Never hardcode UI strings, labels, dimensions, regex patterns, route paths, query keys, filenames, or default values — define in `src/constants/`.
- Never hardcode application routes — use `src/constants/routes.ts`.
- Never hardcode API base URLs — use environment variables.
- Keep API endpoints centralized in `src/constants/api.ts`.

## Styling
- Never use inline styles — use Tailwind utility classes or design tokens.
- Use `cn()` utility from `src/lib/utils/cn.ts` for conditional and dynamic class composition.
- Use shadcn/ui for all common UI primitives.
- Place reusable UI in `src/components/shared/`; feature-specific in `src/components/features/<feature>/`.
- Follow mobile-first responsive design (base styles → sm → md → lg → xl).

## TypeScript
- Keep types, interfaces, enums, DTOs, and component props in `src/types/` — never inline in component files.
- Use strict TypeScript; avoid `any`.

## Data Fetching
- Create reusable custom hooks in `src/hooks/` for data fetching and business logic.
- Use TanStack Query for all client-side data fetching.

## Quality
- Follow accessibility best practices (semantic HTML, aria attributes, keyboard navigation).
- Minimize unnecessary re-renders; avoid redundant computations.
- Maintain consistent naming conventions across components, hooks, utilities, and constants.
- Write clean, readable, maintainable, and scalable code.
